Important correction before executing the ATM code
There is one Java compilation detail in the earlier source code: Scanner(File) only declares FileNotFoundException, so the separate IOException catch needs an operation that can actually throw IOException.

To make both file-related catch blocks valid, replace the card-reader checking section with:
try (java.io.BufferedReader reader =
         new java.io.BufferedReader(
             new java.io.FileReader(file))) {
    reader.readLine();
}


Also, replace the multi-catch print statement with:
System.out.println(
    "Invalid input. Please enter valid numeric values."
);


This avoids displaying null for the InputMismatchException message.

